DTSTAMP:20261126T212723Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20261210T210000
SUMMARY:RESCHEDULED Break into Tech Sales: Career Pivot Workshop (BALLPARK)
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free ($40 value)\n\n🔁 RESCHEDULED: now Thursday\, Dec
 ember 10\, 6–9pm at Thrive Workplace (Ballpark)\n\n🎟️ Entry is FREE
  ($40 value)\, covered by our sponsor. Space is limited to 40 attendees\, 
 so please RSVP to save your spot.\n\n🗓 Thursday\, December 10\n🕕 6:0
 0 – 9:00 PM\n📍 Thrive Workplace\, 1415 Park Avenue West\, Denver\, CO
  80205 (Ballpark)\n\nWant to break into tech but don't have a technical ba
 ckground?\nYou don't need to know how to code to build a career in technol
 ogy.\nThis hands-on training workshop is designed for people considering a
  career change who want to understand how tech sales actually works\, how 
 to land an entry-level sales role\, how to succeed once you're hired\, and
  how that first job can turn into a six-figure career path.\nWe'll walk th
 rough the entire tech sales career ladder—from Sales Development Represe
 ntative (SDR) to Account Executive (AE) to Enterprise and Strategic Sales
 —as well as alternative career paths including Customer Success\, Accoun
 t Management\, Partnerships\, Sales Operations\, Sales Engineering\, and l
 eadership.\nYou'll also learn the actual day-to-day skills companies expec
 t from entry-level salespeople so that you can start developing experience
  before someone gives you your first traditional tech sales job.\n\nWhat I
 s Tech Sales?\n\nMost technology companies—especially software and SaaS 
 companies—need sales teams to find potential customers\, understand thei
 r problems\, demonstrate how the company's product can help\, negotiate co
 ntracts\, and ultimately generate revenue.\nUnlike retail sales\, many tec
 hnology sales jobs are structured around a base salary + commission.\nYou'
 ll often hear the term OTE\, or On-Target Earnings. This represents approx
 imately what you could earn if you hit 100% of your sales quota.\nFor exam
 ple:\n$70\,000 base salary + $30\,000 variable commission = $100\,000 OTE.
 \nHigh performers may earn more than OTE\, while salespeople who miss quot
 a may earn significantly less.\n\nThe Tech Sales Career Path\n\nSales Deve
 lopment Representative — SDR / BDR\n\nFor many people entering tech sale
 s\, this is where the journey begins.\nA Sales Development Representative 
 (SDR) or Business Development Representative (BDR) is responsible for find
 ing potential customers and starting conversations with them.\nYou'll lear
 n how SDRs:\n\nResearch companies and decision-makers\, Identify potential
  customers\, Write cold emails\, Make cold calls\, Use LinkedIn for prospe
 cting\, Personalize outreach\, Handle objections\, Qualify prospects\, Sch
 edule meetings for Account Executives\, Work with tools like CRMs and sale
 s-engagement platforms\, Manage activity and pipeline metrics\, Get measur
 ed against quotas.\n\nThis is one of the best places to learn the fundamen
 tals of professional B2B selling.\nAs of August 2026\, RepVue reports a me
 dian Denver SDR base salary of about $60\,000 with approximately $85\,000 
 OTE.\nFor Denver\, a reasonable general range to expect is approximately:\
 n$50\,000–$70\,000 base\n$70\,000–$100\,000+ OTE\nCompensation varies 
 dramatically by company\, industry\, quota\, commission structure\, and ex
 perience.\n\nAccount Executive — Your First Closing Role\n\nThe next maj
 or step is typically becoming an Account Executive (AE).\nInstead of prima
 rily generating meetings\, Account Executives are responsible for turning 
 opportunities into paying customers.\nYou'll learn how AEs:\n\nRun discove
 ry calls\, Identify business problems\, Ask effective sales questions\, De
 liver product demonstrations\, Build business cases\, Navigate multiple st
 akeholders\, Handle objections\, Negotiate pricing\, Manage procurement\, 
 Work through security and legal reviews\, Forecast deals\, Manage a sales 
 pipeline\, Close contracts.\n\nAccount Executive roles are generally divid
 ed based on the size and complexity of the customers they sell to.\n\nWhat
  You'll Learn in This Workshop\n\nWe'll break down the practical skills so
 meone needs to begin working in tech sales\, including:\n\nHow SaaS and te
 chnology companies make money\, Understanding SDR\, BDR\, AE\, Customer Su
 ccess\, and related roles\, Prospecting and account research\, Identifying
  ideal customers\, Finding decision-makers\, Cold emailing\, Cold calling\
 , LinkedIn outreach\, Writing compelling messaging\, Handling rejection\, 
 Asking discovery questions\, Understanding business problems\, Qualifying 
 opportunities\, CRM basics\, Pipeline management\, Sales metrics and quota
 s\, Understanding commission plans\, Interviewing for sales jobs\, Demonst
 rating sales ability without previous tech experience\, Building your firs
 t sales résumé\, Getting promoted from SDR to AE\, Navigating the SMB 
 → Mid-Market → Enterprise → Strategic career path\, Identifying alte
 rnative career paths within technology.\n\nMost importantly\, we'll talk a
 bout what actually makes someone successful in the job after they get hire
 d—not simply how to interview well enough to get hired.\n\nNeed Experien
 ce? You'll Have an Opportunity to Start Building It.\n\nOne of the hardest
  parts of changing careers is the classic problem:\nYou need experience to
  get the job\, but you need the job to get experience.\nParticipants who a
 re interested will receive access to commission-only sales opportunities t
 hey can potentially begin pursuing immediately.\nThese opportunities can g
 ive you a chance to practice skills such as:\n\nProspecting\, Cold outreac
 h\, Lead generation\, Discovery\, Objection handling\, Pipeline building\,
  Selling\, Closing.\n\nParticipation is completely optional.\nCommission-o
 nly work means there is no guaranteed salary or guaranteed income—you ar
 e paid based on the applicable compensation structure and results.\nFor so
 meone starting from zero\, however\, it can provide an opportunity to begi
 n building real-world experience and a track record to discuss in future i
 nterviews.\n\n⚠️ Important: This Is Training\, Not a Job Guarantee\n\n
 Purchasing a ticket or completing this workshop does NOT guarantee employm
 ent\, a salaried position\, interviews\, commissions\, promotions\, or any
  particular level of income.\nTech sales can be competitive.\nCompanies ma
 ke their own hiring decisions\, and factors including the economy\, job ma
 rket\, experience\, interview performance\, location\, individual performa
 nce\, and company hiring requirements can affect your ability to secure a 
 role.\nSalary ranges discussed during the workshop are examples and market
  estimates—not promises of compensation.\nThe goal of this program is to
  give you:\nKnowledge. Skills. Practice. Resources. A roadmap. And a way t
 o begin building experience.\nWhat you do with those tools is ultimately u
 p to you.\n\nWho Should Attend?\n\nThis workshop is designed for people wh
 o are:\n\nConsidering a career change\, Interested in technology but don't
  know how to code\, Coming from hospitality\, retail\, education\, custome
 r service\, recruiting\, healthcare\, nonprofit work\, entrepreneurship\, 
 or another industry\, Recent college graduates\, Returning to the workforc
 e\, Interested in increasing their earning potential\, Curious about SaaS 
 careers\, Already in sales but trying to move into technology\, Interested
  in Customer Success or other customer-facing tech careers\, Willing to le
 arn\, practice\, hear “no\,” and keep improving.\n\nYou don't need a c
 omputer science degree.\nYou don't need to know how to code.\nAnd you don'
 t necessarily need previous technology experience.\nYou do need to be will
 ing to communicate\, learn\, practice\, accept feedback\, and put in the w
 ork.\nIf you've been looking at tech salaries from the outside wondering 
 “How do people actually get into these jobs?”—this workshop is desig
 ned to show you the path.\n\nRSVP or application may be required. Calendar
  listing does not register you.\n\nhttps://mingledenver.com/events/resched
 uled-break-into-tech-sales-career-pivot-workshop-ball-eadeda3c
LOCATION:Thrive Workplace\, 1415 Park Avenue West\, Denver\, CO 80205
URL:https://mingledenver.com/events/rescheduled-break-into-tech-sales-caree
 r-pivot-workshop-ball-eadeda3c
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
